# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

## [Unreleased]

### Added
  - `CaptureStats` (`core::stats`): running capture statistics (packet count,
    bytes, first/last timestamp) computed in constant memory
  - `PcapError::Truncated`: a capture that ends in the middle of a packet is
    reported as truncated instead of a generic read error
  - `PacketId` (`core::packet`): identity of a packet, its position in the
    capture numbered from 1 like Wireshark frame numbers; `RawPacket::id()`
  - `protocols` module, with the protocol number types `EtherType` and
    `IpProtocol` (known values as constants, e.g. `IpProtocol::TCP`)
  - `Span` (`protocols`): position of a header in the raw bytes of its packet
  - `Stop` and `HeaderKind` (`protocols`): why decoding of a packet ended early
    (truncated, malformed, unsupported protocol, too many nested headers)
  - `LinkType` implements `Hash`

### Fixed
  - `onx read` streams packets instead of loading the whole capture in memory
    (1 GB capture: peak RSS 1.19 GB -> 10 MB)
  - `onx read` keeps and reports the packets read before an error, then exits
    with status 1, instead of discarding them

### Changed
  - **Breaking:** `NxPacket` renamed to `RawPacket`, `NxPacketFormat` to `DisplayFormat`,
    `NxPacketDisplay` to `RawPacketDisplay`. Library types no longer carry the `Nx`
    prefix: modules namespace them (`onx::core::packet::RawPacket`).
  - **Breaking:** `RawPacket::new` takes a `PacketId` as its first argument.

## [0.0.2] - 2026-02-15

### Added
  - PCAP and PCAPNG file reading
  - `NxPacket` struct for unified packet representation
  - `PacketSource` trait for capture abstraction
  - Basic CLI with `read` command
  - Integration tests with sample PCAP files
  
  ### Dependencies
  - Added pcap-file 3.0.0-rc1
  - Added thiserror 2.0.18
  - Added clap 4.5
  - Added time 0.3

## [0.0.1] - 2026-01-31

### Added
- Initial project structure
- Workspace setup with `onx` crate
- MIT OR Apache-2.0 dual licensing
- Placeholder binary for crate name reservation

### Notes
This is a name reservation release. Core functionality will be implemented
in v0.1.0.
